sudo git clone https://github.com/digininja/DVWA.git

Step 1: Navigate to the Web Root Directory
Open the terminal and move to the Apache web server directory.
Command:
$ cd /var/www/html
$ ls
Step 2: Download the DVWA Application
Verify that the project has been downloaded.
$ ls
Rename the folder.
$ sudo mv DVWA dvwa
Provide the necessary permissions.
$ sudo chmod -R 777 dvwa
Step 3: Configure DVWA
Move to the DVWA configuration directory.
$ cd dvwa
$ ls
$ cd config
Check the available files.
$ ls
Copy the configuration template.
$ sudo cp config.inc.php.dist config.inc.php
Edit the configuration file.
$ sudo nano config.inc.php
Modify the following database settings:
$_DVWA['db_server']   = '127.0.0.1';
$_DVWA['db_database'] = 'dvwa';
$_DVWA['db_user']     = 'admin';
$_DVWA['db_password'] = 'password';
Save the file.
Verify the configuration.
$ sudo cat config.inc.php
Step 4: Start the Database Server
Start the MySQL service.
$ sudo service mysql start
Login as the root user.
$ sudo mysql -u root -p
Create the DVWA database.
> Create database dvwa;
Create a database user.
> Create user admin@localhost identified by 'password';
Grant privileges.
> grant all on dvwa.* to admin@localhost;
/*
Apply the changes.
> FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
*/
Exit MySQL.
> exit;

Step 5: Configure PHP
Navigate to the PHP configuration directory.
$ cd /etc/php/8.4/apache2
$ ls
Open the PHP configuration file.
$ sudo nano php.ini
Modify the required PHP settings (allow_ul_include=ON), save the file, and exit.
Step 6: Start Apache and MySQL Services
Start the Apache web server.
$ sudo service apache2 start
Ensure that the database service is running.
$ sudo service mysql start

Step 7: Open DVWA in the Browser
Open a web browser and enter:
http://localhost/dvwa
Login using the default credentials:
•	Username: admin 
•	Password: password 
Click Create/Reset Database.
Step 8: Configure the Security Level
1.	Login to DVWA. 
2.	Select DVWA Security. 
3.	Change the security level to Low. 
4.	Click Submit. 
